ther apparel. It also offers sports apparel, performance leggings and tops, super-soft pima cotton tops, vests, fleeces, and jackets; and necessities comprising scrub caps, lanyards, badge reels, bags, baseball caps, and beanies. The company markets and sells its products to healthcare professionals through its direct-to-consumer digital platform comprising website, mobile app, and B2B business, as well as retail stores. FIGS, Inc. was incorporated in 2013 and is headquartered in Santa Monica, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Catherine Eva Spear | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 330 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $161K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $81K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["FIGS, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.3B market cap on $631M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 10% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 69% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $53M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.79\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 230% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.2986797126201286},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 14% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FIGS (FIGS) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/figs-figs-q3-2026-earnings-085842000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793956239.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"FIGS (FIGS) Stock Looks Above Fair Value On Its 245% Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-figs/figs/news/figs-figs-stock-looks-above-fair-value-on-its-245-run","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793950079.726,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Signet Jewelers (NYSE:SIG) vs. FIGS (NYSE:FIGS) Financial Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/signet-jewelers-nysesig-vs-figs-nysefigs-financial-survey.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793935728.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Figs (FIGS) Tops Q3 Earnings and Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025114/figs-figs-tops-q3-earnings-and-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3025114","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793923207.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Compared to Estimates, Figs (FIGS) Q3 Earnings: A Look at Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024986/compared-to-estimates-figs-figs-q3-earnings-a-look-at-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3024986","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793919603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"FIGS GAAP EPS of $0.10 beats by $0.03, revenue 