ast sell-offs it fell 78% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $6.01 (margin of safety -230%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 50%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $4.92 to $7.62 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 60.1 vs 19.3, EV/EBITDA 33.8 vs 11.2 and P/FCF 62.1 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 78% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 1.6% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 1.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 8 covering analysts target $21.12 on average, 7% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 14% earns above the cost of capital of 10.2%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.61).","It runs a 69% gross margin and converts 8% of revenue into free cash flow, or 4% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.79x.","ROE of 8% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 4.3% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $300.8M (2% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 16.1, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 4.94).","Working capital ties up about 193 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 7.7% over 3 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 13.6% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 13%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 1.3% of sales), a maintenance pace.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 141.3% on average.","Analysts expect 4.5% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.5%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Short interest is elevated at 21.8% of the float, 5.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 330 employees, each generates about $1.9M of revenue, 5.0x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 10.7% a year.","That works out to $161K of free cash flow per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $3.5M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $81K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":57,"head":"Avoid: priced 230% above its fair value of $6.01.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 40, gates 8/25)","Revenue grew 7.7%/yr over 3y","Net cash of $300.8M","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +88%"],"cons":["Trades 230% above fair value of $6.01","P/E 60.1x vs sector 19.3x","EV/EBITDA 33.8x vs sector 11.2x","P/FCF 62.1x vs sector 16.5x"],"flags":["Priced 230% above its fair value of $6.01"],"need":[],"buy_below":5.11,"vc":{"base":6.01,"base_src":"dcf","bear":4.92,"bull":7.62,"alt_median":2.97,"n_alt":2,"gap":1.0223,"dispersion":0.4988,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (50% dispersion)","DCF is 102% above the other models' median ($2.97)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"FIGS","date":"2026-11-06"}